NAME
    fg - wait for a background job and copy its retained output

SYNOPSIS
    fg JOB

DESCRIPTION
    Attaches to one session-owned job until it exits, is cancelled, or faults.
    The job's bounded recent output is copied before its terminal record is
    reaped. JOB is the number printed when the command was started with &.

    Standard input is bound when a job is launched, so a backgrounded command
    keeps reading an empty stream and observing end of input. fg waits for the
    job; it does not hand it the session terminal.
